Hiya, Carol.

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:17.510
Hi, LeVar.

00:24:17.650 --> 00:24:18.410
What are you up to here?

00:24:18.530 --> 00:24:20.410
Well, I'm teaching this newborn baby how to drink.

00:24:20.610 --> 00:24:21.990
A newborn? How old is she?

00:24:22.110 --> 00:24:23.450
She's approximately one day old.

00:24:23.650 --> 00:24:26.350
Oh, come on, you're kidding. She's awfully big for a day old.

00:24:26.490 --> 00:24:29.610
She weighs about 150 pounds. That's pretty big. Isn't it for a newborn one?

00:24:29.790 --> 00:24:29.810
Sure.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.780
is. Now, it looks like you're feeding her milk here, but is there something special that you give

00:24:33.780 --> 00:24:37.560
the baby calves in the milk? This is cholesterol, LeVar. This is the first milk that comes from the

00:24:37.560 --> 00:24:41.900
mother cow. And it's very important that the baby calf gets this milk because it contains a lot of

00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:45.900
antibodies that keeps the baby from getting sick. Now, these are antibodies from the mother,

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:49.540
especially for this calf, huh? Especially from her own mother, that's right. And that keeps her

00:24:49.540 --> 00:24:53.760
healthy, huh? That's right. So, how do you tell if a calf is sick? Well, you can tell if a calf is sick

00:24:53.760 --> 00:24:58.420
by checking its nose. You can see if the nose is dry. This one's nose is real wet. Yeah, it is.

00:24:58.420 --> 00:24:59.860
Yeah, the eyes are sunken in.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:04.720
ears are droopy those are all signs of those are all signs of a sick calf but this is a very healthy

00:25:04.720 --> 00:25:09.480
calf so these are like your babies these calves right they're all my babies lavar each one has

00:25:09.480 --> 00:25:13.080
their own little personality when i come out in the morning to feed them they say here comes mommy

00:25:13.080 --> 00:25:18.780
we're hungry so they depend on you a lot these babies they sure do and they're very important

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:23.980
because they're our future and approximately two to two and a half years these little babies will

00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:28.820
become cows they'll start producing milk so it keeps the cycle going these babies will grow up

00:25:29.320 --> 00:25:29.680
That's right.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.640
They'll become the milk makers of the future.

00:25:31.760 --> 00:25:32.280
They sure do.

00:25:58.860 --> 00:25:59.980
It's wonderful to know that...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:05.420
most of the milk we drink begins with the miracle of birth, the start of a new life,

00:26:06.230 --> 00:26:07.090
a baby calf.

00:26:07.740 --> 00:26:12.980
Nature provides for all of us through cycles just like this one, and one of nature's most

00:26:12.980 --> 00:26:17.050
remarkable cycles is the story of the milk makers.

